        ("hard", "Explain widget lifecycle in Flutter and when to use const constructors.",
         "Widgets are immutable descriptions rebuilt by the framework, with create, initState, didUpdateWidget, build, and dispose hooks. A const constructor canonicalizes identical widgets so the element tree can skip rebuilding identical subtrees, which is a real performance win."),
