        ("easy", "What is the difference between `>` and `>>` redirection?",
         "`>` truncates and writes the file, while `>>` appends. Both write stdout unless a file descriptor is specified with 2> for stderr."),
        ("easy", "How do you pass arguments to a bash script and read them?",
         "Positional parameters are $1, $2, and so on, with $# the count, $@ the arguments as an array, and $0 the script name. Always quote \"$@\" to preserve argument boundaries."),
